        "test_sequence": 14,
        "message": "Blueprint.__init__ now raises ValueError(\"'name' may not be empty.\") when name is empty/falsy, placed immediately before the existing dot-name check. This makes empty blueprint names fail fast at construction instead of misbehaving later (issue #4944). Added focused regression test test_blueprint_name_validation asserting: empty name raises the new ValueError, dotted name still raises the original error, and a valid name still constructs.\n\nChanged files (patch-2, version v3): src/flask/blueprints.py (3 lines), tests/test_blueprints.py (test only).\n\nEvidence on this exact version v3: focused test 1 collected/1 passed; full tests/test_blueprints.py 60 collected, 60 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors, validation_status verified. The pre-fix 59-test run did not exercise this behavior; the added test is what actually covers the issue-specific path.\n\nUnverified: no hidden acceptance tests were run; a public pass is not acceptance.",
